# Day 02 – Git & GitHub Practice Session

## 1. Linux / Git Bash Commands Practiced

* `cd` — Change the current directory.
* `cd ..` — Move one directory back.
* `ls` — List files and folders.
* `ls -a` — Show all files, including hidden files.
* `mkdir` — Create a new directory/folder.
* `touch` — Create a new empty file.
* `rm -f` — Remove a file.
* `rm -r` — Remove a directory recursively.
* `rm -rf` — Forcefully remove a directory and its contents.
* `cat` — Display the contents of a file.
* `cat > file.txt` — Create/overwrite a file with terminal input.
* `cat >> file.txt` — Append content to an existing file.
* `vi` — Open/edit a file from the terminal.
* `pwd` — Display the current working directory.
* `history` — Display previously executed Bash commands.
* `history > daytwo` — Save terminal command history into a file named `daytwo`.
* `cp` — Copy files or directories.
* `mv` — Move or rename files/directories.

