## 12. Important Git Concepts Learned

### Working Directory

The place where I create and modify files.

### Staging Area

The place where I select changes that should go into the next commit.

### Local Repository

The `.git` database on my computer containing Git commits and history.

### Remote Repository

The repository hosted on GitHub.

### Commit

A saved snapshot of staged changes.

### Branch

A movable pointer representing a line of development.

### HEAD

A pointer that tells Git where I am currently working, normally pointing to the current branch.

Example:

```text
HEAD → main → latest commit
```

---

## 13. Main Workflow Learned

The most important Git workflow from today's practice:

```text
Create / Modify File
        ↓
   git status
        ↓
     git add
        ↓
   Staging Area
        ↓
   git commit
        ↓
 Local Repository
        ↓
     git push
        ↓
      GitHub
```

If GitHub has newer changes:

```text
git pull --rebase origin main
        ↓
     git push
```

