## 14. Key Lessons From Today's Mistakes

* I learned that I don't need to clone the repository every day.
* I only need to clone a repository when creating a local copy for the first time.
* After that, I can continue working inside the existing local repository.
* `git add` is used before `git commit`.
* `git commit` saves staged changes locally.
* `git push` uploads local commits to GitHub.
* `git pull` gets changes from GitHub.
* I learned how to unstage a file using `git restore --staged`.
* I learned why filenames containing spaces or special characters should be placed inside quotes.
* I learned how to check the repository state using `git status`.
* I learned how to view commit history using `git log` and `git log --oneline`.
* I practiced moving a branch back to an earlier commit using `git reset`.
* I learned that a rejected push can happen when the remote repository contains commits that my local repository does not have.
* I learned to synchronize with the remote repository before pushing when this happens.

